Commands
git --version
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/YOUR-REPOSITORY.git
git push -u origin main








--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Steps to run:
1. Install Git and create an empty repository on GitHub.
2. Open a terminal in your project directory.
3. Run the commands above in order, replacing the remote URL with your repository URL.
4. If Git asks for identity, set it with git config --global user.name "Your Name" and git config --global user.email "you@example.com".
5. Complete GitHub authentication when prompted. Do not put passwords or access tokens directly into source files.
